From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: the split's back runs an instance loop's run of identical draw.begin entries as one (EDEN_UP_INSTANCE_RUNS=1), off by default

Upstream: zortos293/Lichii PR #1597 (head e6f9107cc5, by sanchodecuba11-del with Claude), +36 lines
in maxwell_3d.cpp/.h and gpu_split.cpp. Not merged: the author closed it on 13 Nov after a retest
on nx2 87d84d513c showed no fps difference while moving ("the 27 -> 31 fps in the description was
run-to-run variation"); it saves about 16 ms/s of the back on his PC (Ryzen 7 5800X), about 2%.
Ported anyway as a test arm: our frame time is set by the CPU side and our cores are slower.

What: with EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP=1 (0600, #178 + #488) the split front sends no draw.end inside an
instance loop, so the loop's draw.begin writes reach the back as runs of identical one-word Method
entries; each ran the whole CallMethod path to add one instance (upstream counted ~770,000 a
second for ~56,000 draws in the village, moving). GpuSplit::Execute now, for a Maxwell3D with
repeat_draw_begin, finds such a run (same 64-bit head, no DMA segment word, within the words the
front published and before the ring's end), runs the first entry as before and adds the others'
instances at once through Maxwell3D::RepeatDrawBegin. That does it only where a begin would do
nothing else: no macro collecting parameters, regs.draw.instance_id Subsequent and the draw
manager already in DrawMode::Instance after the first; else it returns false and the back runs
CallMethod for each entry, as before. Ported differences: our Execute is engine-generic (the
engine flag repeat_draw_begin marks the Maxwell3D, as batch_constant_words does); upstream's
fast_maxwell3d and EDEN_NX2_PERF_VERIFY checks have no counterpart here; the write history
(EDEN_NX2_3D_HISTORY) keeps every write (the switch is off with it); with EDEN_NX2_GPU_PROFILE the
merged writes are still counted as method writes.
Read in our tree that a repeated subsequent begin changes nothing else: ProcessShadowRam gives the
same value (Track stores it, Replay reads it), WriteDirtyRegister flushes no deferred draw for an
instance-loop method and breaks no fast draw for an unchanged value, ProcessMethodCall breaks no
fast draw for it and DrawManager::DrawBegin only does instance_count++, mode Instance and topology
from the unchanged register.

Needs: EDEN_UP_LOOP_SKIP=1 with the split (EDEN_NX2_SPLIT=2) and the same-value skip on; without
LOOP_SKIP the front sends draw.end between the begins, runs are rare and nothing changes (a line at
start says so).
Off (unset or anything but "1"): one plain bool load per Method entry on the back, nothing else.

